From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EvilMetaMonkey <hood.mj85@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 01:55:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 13/31] Refuse checkpoint restore and redo of Git-ignored paths

In a Git work tree, the planner asks git check-ignore (one batch per
plan) which checkpoint paths Git ignores now, and reports each as a
git_ignored conflict, so restore and redo never create, overwrite or
delete a Git-ignored file. A missing or failing git returns
git_unavailable or git_failed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 lib/src/checkpoint_plan.dart            | 15 +++++++++++++++
 lib/src/checkpoint_restore_service.dart | 22 ++++++++++++++++++----
 2 files changed, 33 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

